const e="tirana-airport-car-rental-guide",a="Car Rental at Tirana Airport: A Complete Pickup Guide for 2026",t="Car Rental Tirana Airport: Pickup Guide & Tips",r="Car rental at Tirana Airport made simple: how meet & greet pickup works, documents you need, inspection tips and routes to Tirana or the coast. Book ahead.",o="Everything you need to know about renting a car at Tirana International Airport: pickup, documents, inspection, insurance and the drive to Tirana or the coast.",n=["car rental Tirana airport","rent a car Tirana airport","Tirana airport car hire","TIA car rental pickup","documents to rent a car in Albania","Tirana airport to city centre by car"],l=5,i=`<p>Renting a car at Tirana International Airport (TIA) is the easiest way to start an Albania trip: you land, meet your rental agent in the arrivals area, sign, and drive off within minutes. This guide explains how pickup works with Rent Ride, which documents to bring, what to check before you leave the car park and how long the drive takes to Tirana, Durrës or the southern coast.</p><h2>Why rent a car at Tirana airport?</h2><p>Tirana International Airport Nënë Tereza, often called Mother Teresa Airport or simply TIA, is Albania's main international gateway. It sits at Rinas, roughly 17 km northwest of central Tirana. Public transport from the airport is limited to a shuttle bus into the city and taxis, which works for a city break but not for exploring the country. Many of Albania's highlights, such as Berat, Gjirokastër, the Riviera beaches and the northern Alps, are spread out and poorly connected by bus. A car gives you the freedom to stop at viewpoints, reach beaches that buses never visit and travel on your own schedule.</p><p>Collecting the car directly at the airport also saves you a taxi fare and a second trip into town. You go straight from the terminal to the motorway.</p><h2>How pickup works with Rent Ride</h2><p>Rent Ride works on a <strong>meet &amp; greet</strong> basis at the airport, and delivery and collection at TIA are free. Here is what to expect:</p><ol><li><strong>Book online.</strong> Choose your car, dates, insurance level and any extras on the booking page. Add your flight number so the team can follow your arrival time.</li><li><strong>Land and clear passport control.</strong> Collect your luggage as usual.</li><li><strong>Meet your agent in arrivals.</strong> A Rent Ride representative waits for you in the arrivals hall. If your flight is delayed, the team sees it and adjusts.</li><li><strong>Walk to the car.</strong> The car is parked close to the terminal. You check it together, sign the agreement and receive the keys.</li><li><strong>Drive away.</strong> The whole handover usually takes far less time than queuing at a traditional rental desk.</li></ol><p>Service runs 24/7, so late-night and early-morning flights are covered. Returns work the same way in reverse: you bring the car back to the airport, an agent checks it with you, and you walk into departures. If you are staying in Tirana first and only need the car later, free delivery to the Tirana city centre is also available through our Tirana car rental service.</p><h2>Documents you need to rent a car in Albania</h2><p>Bring the following to the pickup:</p><ul><li><strong>A valid driving licence</strong> that you have held for at least one year. EU and other international licences are accepted.</li><li><strong>A passport or national ID card.</strong></li><li><strong>Your booking confirmation</strong>, on your phone is fine.</li></ul><p>The minimum rental age is 21. Drivers between 21 and 25 may pay a young-driver surcharge depending on the car category. Every person who will drive must be named on the rental agreement, so add an extra driver at booking if you plan to share the driving.</p><p>If your licence is not printed in the Latin alphabet, contact us before you travel to confirm whether you should also carry an International Driving Permit. Rent Ride does not require a security deposit, so there is no large amount blocked on your card for the duration of the trip.</p><h2>Choosing the right car for your trip</h2><p>The right category depends on where you are going:</p><ul><li><strong>Economy cars</strong> are ideal for couples and for city driving, coastal towns and narrow old-town streets where parking is tight. Prices start from €25/day.</li><li><strong>SUVs</strong> make sense for families, lots of luggage, and mountain areas such as Theth or remote beaches with rough access tracks. See our <a href="/makina-suv-me-qira">SUV rentals</a>.</li><li><strong>Automatic cars</strong> are worth booking early if you are not used to a manual gearbox, especially for steep mountain roads and hill starts in towns like Gjirokastër. Browse automatic cars.</li></ul><p>Child seats, GPS and other equipment can be added during booking. You can compare every model on the fleet page.</p><h2>Inspection tips before you drive off</h2><p>A few minutes of checking at pickup prevents misunderstandings at return:</p><ul><li><strong>Walk around the car with the agent</strong> and make sure every existing scratch or dent is marked on the check-out sheet.</li><li><strong>Take photos and a short video</strong> of all four sides, the wheels, the windscreen and the interior. Make sure your phone records the date.</li><li><strong>Check the fuel gauge.</strong> Cars are handed over with a full tank and should be returned full.</li><li><strong>Test the basics:</strong> lights, wipers, air conditioning (essential in an Albanian summer) and the horn.</li><li><strong>Look at the tyres</strong>, including the spare if there is one, and ask where the warning triangle and safety vest are kept.</li><li><strong>Save the 24/7 support number</strong>: +355 69 81 45 803, also on WhatsApp.</li></ul><h2>Insurance: what is included</h2><p>Every Rent Ride car includes basic Collision Damage Waiver (CDW), which limits what you pay if the car is damaged to a standard excess. At booking you can upgrade to <strong>Super CDW</strong>, which reduces the excess to zero. Given Albania's narrow coastal roads, tight parking and occasional potholes, many travellers choose full cover for peace of mind. Our article on <a href="/blog/car-rental-insurance-albania-explained">car rental insurance in Albania</a> explains the options in more detail.</p><h2>Driving from Tirana airport: where to next</h2><p>The airport connects to the main SH2 road between Tirana and Durrës, so you are on a good dual carriageway within minutes. Approximate driving times in normal traffic:</p><table><thead><tr><th>Destination</th><th>Approx. distance</th><th>Approx. driving time</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Tirana city centre</td><td>17 km</td><td>20–30 min (longer at rush hour)</td></tr><tr><td>Durrës</td><td>35 km</td><td>30–40 min</td></tr><tr><td>Berat</td><td>120 km</td><td>About 2 hours</td></tr><tr><td>Vlorë</td><td>150 km</td><td>2–2.5 hours</td></tr><tr><td>Shkodër</td><td>100 km</td><td>1.5–2 hours</td></tr><tr><td>Sarandë / Ksamil</td><td>280–300 km</td><td>4.5–5.5 hours</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Times vary with traffic, roadworks and summer congestion, so treat them as a guide rather than a promise.</p><h3>Airport to Tirana city centre</h3><p>Follow signs for Tirana. Traffic in the city can be dense, especially on weekday afternoons, and parking in the centre is limited. If your hotel has parking, confirm it in advance.</p><h3>Airport to the coast</h3><p>To head south, follow signs for Durrës and then the motorway towards Fier and Vlorë. You can avoid central Tirana completely, which makes the airport an ideal starting point for a coastal trip. For a full route south, read our guide to <a href="/blog/tirana-to-ksamil-saranda-by-car">driving from Tirana to Ksamil and Saranda</a>, or plan a longer loop with our Albania road trip itinerary.</p><h2>Booking tips</h2><ul><li><strong>Book early for July and August.</strong> Summer is peak season, and automatics and SUVs go first.</li><li><strong>Flexible plans?</strong> Cancellation is free up to 48 hours before pickup. For later cancellations, up to 50% of the booking value may be retained.</li><li><strong>Planning to visit Montenegro, Kosovo or North Macedonia?</strong> Request a cross-border permit when you book. Our guide on <a href="/blog/crossing-borders-rental-car-albania">crossing borders with a rental car</a> covers the details.</li></ul><h2>Ready to pick up your car at TIA?</h2><p>Renting a car at Tirana airport means your Albania trip starts the moment you land. With free meet &amp; greet delivery, no security deposit and 24/7 support, Rent Ride keeps the process simple. <a href="/makine-me-qira-aeroport">Book your Tirana airport car rental</a> online in a couple of minutes, or message us on WhatsApp if you have any questions before you travel.</p>`,s=[{question:"Is there a Rent Ride desk inside Tirana airport?",answer:"Rent Ride works on a meet & greet basis rather than from a fixed desk. A representative waits for you in the arrivals hall, walks you to the car parked near the terminal, and completes the handover with you. Delivery and return at the airport are free, and the service runs 24/7, including night flights."},{question:"What happens if my flight to Tirana is delayed?",answer:"Add your flight number when you book. The team follows your arrival time and adjusts the meeting accordingly, so a delay does not mean losing your car. If anything changes at short notice, you can reach 24/7 support by phone or WhatsApp on +355 69 81 45 803."},{question:"Do I need a credit card or a deposit to rent a car at Tirana airport?",answer:"Rent Ride does not require a security deposit, so no large amount is blocked on your card during the rental. You need a valid driving licence held for at least one year, a passport or national ID card, and your booking confirmation."},{question:"How long does it take to drive from Tirana airport to the city centre?",answer:"The airport is about 17 km from central Tirana. In normal traffic the drive takes roughly 20 to 30 minutes, but it can take longer during weekday rush hours. Parking in the centre is limited, so check whether your accommodation offers a parking space."},{question:"Can I return the car at Tirana airport at night?",answer:"Yes. Returns at Tirana International Airport are available 24/7, including weekends and public holidays. Let the team know your departure time when booking, return the car with a full tank, and an agent will check it with you before you head to departures."}],h={slug:e,title:a,metaTitle:t,metaDescription:r,excerpt:o,keywords:n,readingMinutes:5,html:i,faq:s};export{h as default,o as excerpt,s as faq,i as html,n as keywords,r as metaDescription,t as metaTitle,l as readingMinutes,e as slug,a as title};
